 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nRequestValidator.authenticate_client_id method no longer raises NotImplementedError\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `authenticate_client_id` method in `RequestValidator` class has been modified and no longer raises `NotImplementedError` when called. This breaks the expected contract for subclasses that rely on this method raising an exception to indicate it must be implemented.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.request_validator import RequestValidator\n\nv = RequestValidator()\n# This should raise NotImplementedError but doesn't anymore\ntry:\n    v.authenticate_client_id('client_id', 'request')\n    print(\"ERROR: No exception raised!\")\nexcept NotImplementedError:\n    print(\"Expected: NotImplementedError raised\")\n```\n\nThe method now returns boolean values instead of raising `NotImplementedError`, which changes the expected behavior for base class implementations.\n</issue>\n",
